        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "The matrix inequality in (1) is understood in the sense of quadratic forms. Therefore, if (1) holds, then multiplying it from the left by  $ u^\\top $ and from the right by  $ u $ gives (2). Conversely, if (2) holds for all normalized  $ u = (a, b) $, then the last identity gives the same lower bound for all normalized quadratic forms of  $ G_T $. This is precisely (1).",
            "block_bbox": [
                137,
